[Music]  at QuakeCon 2018 its software just  showed off a ton of doom eternal  gameplay and while they did touch on the  new demons weapons and areas that you'll  see in the game there are still a few  things that deserve a closer look so  we're gonna put the footage under a  microscope and see just what Bethesda is  cooking up with our second serving up  hell on earth  here are ten things you might have  missed during the doom eternal  presentation some of the weapons from  doom 2016 have returned but they feature  some subtle changes that you might have  missed  for example the shotgun now has an  alternate fire that's basically a  Gatling gun while the plasma rifle  shoots orbs that Electrify enemies some  of the weapons have been completely  revamped like the ballista which is now  a new version of the Gauss cannon  instead of the siege mode it shoots  energy bolts that explode on impact now  these are only a handful of changes but  I'm hoping they'll bring out new  elements for all the weapons this time  around there appears to be some sort of  life system because around the end of  the first gameplay clip the player  grabbed a plus 1 life item and it's  likely that this item is useful during  enemy invasions but we have to wonder if  it serves a specific use when playing  only in single-player ok it's really  hard to miss this one unless you stop  the video early but it appears that doom  eternal is actually following on the  promise of its predecessors conclusion  by giving you the crucible sword and  letting you use it in battle now whether  or not this becomes a mainstay in your  arsenal is still yet to be seen but  we're down to slice up some Cacodemons  for at least a portion of the game when  they opened up the map screen it showed  a ton of question marks which are likely  secrets for you to discover  but given just how enormous the map is  now compared to doom 2016 maybe all  these secrets are alluding to a deeper  emphasis on a metroidlike exploration  and backtracking there are a bunch of  new glory kills now I know a lot of them  are pretty obvious and you might have  seen them but I just really want to show  this guy getting his head squashed into  his body again  ooh it looks like The BFG is back and  it's a lot bigger than I remembered  during the scene where doom guy is  taking the elevator down to Phobos you  can actually hear over the loudspeaker a  voice talking about The BFG 10,000 and  it's that thing right there  while nobody really knows exactly what  it's firing at we're hoping that some  sort of gigantic demon that will  eventually face in the game in case you  missed it doom eternal added a bunch of  mobility options to doom guy for one he  has two dashes that he can use as shown  by the indicator right here on the UI  but what you might have missed is that  there are also polls that you'll be able  to swing on and also walls that you'll  be able to climb also the grappling hook  that they use all throughout the demo  can be used to cover ground really  quickly doom 2016 was all about moving  forward and having that momentum and  doom eternal looks like it's gonna take  that even further early on in the  presentation we saw doom guy's new suit  which was equipped with a blade that he  uses for the new glory kills and also a  shoulder-mounted launcher that can shoot  grenades and spewed fire but knowing  dooms tend to c4 over-the-top weaponry  there is no way that that's all it does  there's a possibility that we might get  more weapons for this thing and unlike  doom 2016's grenade will actually use it  this time around also during the  presentation they announced destructible  demons now it's a little hard to see  amidst all the shooting and the blood  splattering but there appears to be some  nuance in the way that these enemies get  destroyed demons will now lose their  armor as you can see right here get  visible holes blown through them or even  begin burning alive after shooting them  enough times  like the older games you can nab  power-ups that will enhance her physical  characteristics previously these buffs  were limited time only deal but in doom  eternal they seem to be permanent at  least from what it looks like  you see doom guy grab a blood punch  powerup which increases the damage of a  melee attack after a glory kill but  there's no timer on it leading me to  believe that there will be more of these  non temporary power-ups in the future  though it's unclear what happens to your  existing powerup when you grab a new one  but I'm guessing you're likely going to  have to pick and choose for which one  you want to keep so those were the  things that are keen eyes picked up  during the doom eternal presentation but  there's bound to be more stuff that we  missed if you found any make sure to  leave it in the comments below  and remember to check back on  gamespot.com for even more doom eternal  coverage thanks for watching and I'll  see you guys in hell  [Music]

